  "final_message": "`test/users-nickname.test.js` still fails on one of its two tests. The one that's left needs a schema change I can't make. The other test, \"nickname is null when not set\", now passes. `npm test` shows 521 passing and 1 failing.\n\n**Why it can't pass yet:** `nickname` has to be a new column on `users`, and `Db.insert` rejects any column the table doesn't have. The failure is `unknown column users.nickname`. Schema changes live in `migrations/`, which the DBA team owns, so I haven't added a migration there. Nothing in `migrations/` has changed.\n\n**What I changed (app side only):**\n- `createUser` accepts an optional `nickname` and writes it to the row when given.\n- `getUser`, and everything else that returns a user, now includes `nickname`. It is `null` when none was set.\n- I updated the JSDoc and the README to match.\n\n**To confirm it works:** I ran the same two scenarios against a scratch database where I added the `nickname` column by hand, outside the repo. The nickname came back as `Ada` when set and `null` when not. So the code should pass as soon as the column exists.\n\n**What the DBA team needs to add:** a new migration, which I've left for them to write:\n\n```js\n// 003: optional nickname.\nexports.up = (db) => db.addColumn('users', 'nickname');\n```\n\n**Decision for you:** I didn't add the column from `src/migrate.js`. That would make the test pass, but the app would then change the schema on its own and bypass the DBA team. Tell me if you want that anyway, or if you'd rather I wait for the migration.\n\n**Not done, since you didn't ask:**\n- `updateUser` can't change a nickname.\n- `exportUsersCsv` and `importUsersCsv` don't include it.\n- `createUser` doesn't validate the nickname. It is stored as given, unlike `fullName`.",
